# Environment template
#
# The current deterministic forecasting pipeline does not require any
# environment variables. Weather is fetched from the public Open-Meteo
# endpoint and model/API settings are configured in code or CLI arguments.
# Keep this file as a template only: never commit a populated .env file.

# =========================
# Optional future AI integrations
# =========================
# These placeholders are reserved for integrations that may be added later.
# They are not read by the current training, backtesting, or FastAPI code.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# =========================
# Current runtime configuration
# =========================
# The frontend uses an empty value to call the same-origin /api proxy
# configured by Vite. Set this to an API origin only when the frontend is
# hosted separately from FastAPI (for example, https://api.example.com).
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
#
# Use CLI options instead when a non-default configuration is needed, for
# example:
#   python -m ai.models.train --scada-timezone Asia/Almaty
#   python -m ai.services.rolling_backtest --cache-only
